 (ROOT/'reports/CATALOGUE_EXTINCTION_AUDIT.md').write_text('# CATALOGUE AND EXTINCTION AUDIT\n\nSix clusters read directly from arch_code_results/data/hunt24/params.csv; exact centers exported in generated table. Generator source selects nominal-support subsets; NGC188/NGC6791 never enter those subsets. This is distinct from whether a randomly perturbed old-cluster isochrone could ever support a component.\n\nExtinction factors traced to line 43 of both archived forward_model.py copies: (0.789,1.083,0.634). No derivation, citation, or R_V assumption found in retained source. The final manuscript transparently labels these fixed implementation choices, supplies no fabricated citation, and does not assign R_V=3.1 by analogy with prior literature.\n\nOptional tie-breaking, matched-grid and no-noise ablations NOT RUN: raw forward inputs exist locally, but these are new response-building tasks outside the prioritized frozen-response revision. No assertion of negligible ties or causally isolated grid effects is made.\n')
